+<h1>Contrastive SSL Vibration</h1>
+<p class="lede">A SimCLR-style encoder that learns vibration representations without any labels by pulling two augmented views of the same window together and pushing every other window apart. In a plant where failures are rare and unlabelled data is abundant, this is the model that manufactures the labels nobody has.</p>
+<div class="cta">
+<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-contrastive-ssl-vibration">View on GitHub</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/ecosystem.html">25-model ecosystem graph</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md">Platform architecture</a>
+</div>
+</header>
+<p class="note">This page is generated from <code>deployment/models.catalog.json</code> in the reference repository, together with the other 24 model pages, so all 25 agree on numbering, contract and status.</p>
+<h2>Model</h2>
+<ul>
+<li><code>Encoder + projection head from model.py</code></li>
+<li><code>Platform adapter supplies the complete NT-Xent loss the repository omits</code></li>
+</ul>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Encoder</th><td>Shared-weight convolutional / MLP trunk producing one embedding per view</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Projection head</th><td>Small MLP mapping embeddings onto the unit sphere where the contrastive loss is computed</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Loss</th><td>NT-Xent over 2N augmented views with a temperature parameter; upstream ships a partial implementation, completed by the adapter</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>Advanced concepts</h2>
+<p class="note">The ideas this model actually leans on, each stated with its failure mode.</p>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>NT-Xent and temperature</h3>
+<p>The loss is a softmax over cosine similarities scaled by 1/temperature. Temperature controls how hard the model punishes near-miss negatives - too low and training collapses, too high and the representation stops discriminating.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Augmentation defines the invariant</h3>
+<p>You are not learning 'normal vibration'; you are learning whatever the augmentation pipeline refuses to change - jitter, amplitude scaling, time shifts. Choose augmentations that are physically irrelevant and the embedding becomes a fault fingerprint.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>What 'partial' buys you</h3>
+<p>The upstream repository defines the encoder but not the full loss. The platform adapter implements it, which is why this model is marked partial rather than complete: the numbers describe the platform's training loop, not the upstream repo's.</p>
+</div>
+<h2>Platform contract</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Input (adapter view)</th><td>unlabelled vibration windows (two augmented views per sample)</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Output</th><td>extracted_features (embeddings)</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Record format</th><td><code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code></td></tr>
+<tr><th>Typical latency</th><td>4000 ms</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Deployment targets</th><td>cloud, edge_gpu</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Requirements</th><td>torch</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Fallback</th><td>none - leaf model</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Subsystem focus</th><td>whole turbine</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes tool</th><td><code>no direct tool - improves anomaly / diagnose evidence</code></td></tr>
+</table>
+<p class="note">Records follow the shared <code>WTDataSchema</code> (<code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code>). Only <code>timestamp</code>, <code>turbine_id</code> and <code>model_id</code> are required; absence is distinguishable from a zero.</p>
+<h2>Platform layers</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Fusion</th><td>Feature extractor: no vote of its own, improves everyone else's features</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Protocol</th><td>Pretraining uses unlabelled windows only; the linear probe is evaluated on held-out rows so no label leaks backwards</td></tr>
+<tr><th>XAI</th><td>Embeddings power the contrastive healthy-band z-score used by the XAI bundle</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Drift</th><td>Embedding-space drift is the most sensitive early warning the platform has, because it needs no labels</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>How it connects to the other 24</h2>
+<ul class="edges">
+<li><b>17. Quantized MobileNet Edge</b> <span class="note">(m24-quantized-edge)</span> &rarr; unlabelled features for SSL pretraining</li>
+<li>&rarr; <b>01. 1D-CNN Bearing Vibration</b> <span class="note">(m01-1dcnn-bearing)</span> - SSL representations for the bearing classifier</li>
+<li>&rarr; <b>20. SVM-RBF Generator Stator</b> <span class="note">(m12-svm-generator)</span> - SSL representations for the SVM kernel</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>Honest limits</h2><ul class="limits">
+<li>Upstream loss incomplete; performance is attributable to the platform's completed NT-Xent</li>
+<li>No downstream fine-tuning is shipped for every classifier - some consume features as-is</li>
+</ul>
+<p class="note">Fidelity: rung 1 of the fidelity ladder - simulator data, surrogate waveforms where stated, proxy RUL targets, simulator fault labels. Comparable within this collection, not field-validated turbine control.</p>
